OL,3,GNEWSAGuilt 'won't ever go away' for
OL,4,Afamilies caught up in valproate scandal
OL,5,
OL,6,F"Even though I know it's not my fault,
OL,7,Fthe guilt continues and I don't think
OL,8,Fit will ever go away."
OL,10,FEmma Friedmann's son Andrew is one of
OL,11,Fan estimated 20,000 children in UK
OL,12,Fbelieved to have been harmed by the
OL,13,Fepilepsy drug sodium valproate since it
OL,14,Fwas first used to treat the condition
OL,15,Fin the 1970s.
OL,17,FBabies exposed to valproate medicines
OL,18,Fin the womb have a 10% chance of
OL,19,Fdeveloping physical abnormalities and
OL,20,F40% chance of developing cognitive
OL,21,Fproblems, such as learning disabilities
OL,22,Fand autism.
